# Only the app and its frozen bundle are deployed. Everything else is build-time
# tooling, unrelated workstreams, or source data -- none of which a deployment
# may read, and all of which would bloat the function.
#
# Scripts/ goes entirely. Excluding it was what made the first deploy return
# FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED -- the app imported six modules from Scripts/lib --
# but the fix is not a narrower ignore rule. build_bundle.py vendors those
# modules into gallery/bundle/lib/, so the bundle is self-contained and this
# rule cannot strand the app again.
Scripts/

data/
docs/
PRD/
outputs/
generated/
test_data/
tests/
weekly_report/
viz_gallery/
backups/
gallery/cache/
gallery/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
notebooks/
*.ipynb
.env*
